  "explanation": "The question asks 'When was the Croatian money introduced?' and two distinct valid interpretations exist based on the sources. The Croatian kuna was first introduced as the currency of the Independent State of Croatia on 26 July 1941 (supported by D2S5, D3S2, D4S1). Later, the modern kuna was introduced on May 30, 1994, marking a transition from the Croatian dinar (supported by D1S3). These are distinct historical events involving the same name 'kuna' but different contexts and referents. Both answers are valid and complementary."
